---
title: Piciformes
---
# Piciformes

Piciformes is the order containing the woodpeckers of [[picidae]], along with the
toucans, barbets and honeyguides. Nearly all members have zygodactyl feet, with
two toes forward and two back, and nearly all excavate their own cavity in wood
or an earth bank. The order is worldwide except for Australia, Madagascar and the
polar regions.
